    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d684">

                <pb facs="0244" n="1362" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v15p2/pg1362"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/7–953: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Embassy in Korea</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d684-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret<lb/>niact</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-07-09T19:46:00-04:00">July 9, 1953—7:46
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>31. Reference your DTG 091600Z<anchor n="2" xml:id="d684-f2"/> and previous.
                    While Rhee’s letter is not entirely
                    satisfactory it represents great progress from situation that existed at time
                    you undertook your mission and probably is about all we will be able obtain from
                    him at this time. Rather than negotiating and exchanging further correspondence
                    on unsatisfactory portions his letter, subject views yourself and Clark, believe we should tacitly consider his
                    letter satisfactory basis for entering into armistice, leaving detailed problems
                    which it raises for future discussion and negotiation.</p>
                <p>However concur on desirability joint US–ROK
                    statement at time your departure along lines suggested your DTG 091125Z,<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d684-f3"/> and suggest efforts now being directed at obtaining
                        Rhee’s agreement to as satisfactory
                    joint statement as possible. Transmit text to Department prior release time so
                    that public relations aspects can be coordinated.</p>
                <pb facs="0245" n="1363" xml:id="pg1363"/>
                <p>With regard to Rhee’s draft mutual security
                    treaty suggest you inform him Department immediately undertaking careful study
                    his draft and will be prepared conclude negotiations at high level meeting with
                    him to follow armistice.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d684-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d684-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram, drafted by Johnson and
                    cleared with Smith and Dulles, was repeated to Pusan as telegram 31
                    and to Tokyo for Murphy and Clark as 90. It was passed to the Department
                    of Defense for Nash and the JCS.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d684-f2" n="2" xml:id="d684-f2-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic"><ref target="#d684">Supra</ref></hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d684-f3" n="3" xml:id="d684-f3-content">
                <p>Dated July 9, <ref target="#pg1355">p. 1355</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
